#: manual/performance/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:1
msgid "dzmingli_vs_floating performance"
msgstr "dzmingli_vs_floating の性能"

#: manual/performance/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:3
msgid "Measurement environment"
msgstr "計測環境"

#: manual/performance/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:5
msgid "The numbers come from one native release run on an Apple M4 under macOS 26.5 with `moon 0.1.20260703`, `DzmingLi/decimal@0.2.2`, `Luna-Flow/floating@0.7.1` and `Luna-Flow/mare_mark@0.3.0`, recorded on 2026-07-15. CPU frequency was not controlled. The MoonBit 0.10 migration on this branch changes no benchmark logic and the run has not been repeated with the new toolchain. The measurement method is derived on the [design page](../design/dzmingli_vs_floating.md#paired-statistics)."
msgstr "数値は Apple M4、macOS 26.5 上で `moon 0.1.20260703`、`DzmingLi/decimal@0.2.2`、`Luna-Flow/floating@0.7.1`、`Luna-Flow/mare_mark@0.3.0` を使った native リリースビルドでの一回の実行から得たもので、2026-07-15 に記録されました。CPU 周波数は制御していません。このブランチの MoonBit 0.10 への移行はベンチマークのロジックを変えておらず、新しいツールチェーンでの再実行はしていません。計測手法は[設計ページ](../design/dzmingli_vs_floating.md#paired-statistics)で導出しています。"

#: manual/performance/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:13
#: manual/performance/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:7
msgid "Results"
msgstr "結果"

#: manual/performance/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:15
msgid "The current `0.7.1` run contains 1,476 scaling validations, with 1,368 passes and 108 DzmingLi failures. The expanded common-digit run contains 1,368/1,368 successful validations for 19 operations."
msgstr "現在の `0.7.1` run は scaling で 1,476 件を検証し、1,368 件が合格、DzmingLi の 108 件が失敗しました。拡張 common-digits は 19 操作について 1,368/1,368 検証に合格しています。"

#: manual/performance/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:19
msgid "At 1,024 digits, where both implementations still pass the oracle, floating GDA records `0.131–16.798 µs/op` for the five arithmetic-only operations versus DzmingLi's `12.459–78.978 µs/op`. Full-path medians are `7.427–24.133 µs/op` versus `152.145–205.549 µs/op`. The resulting GDA speedup ranges from `3.54×` for arithmetic-only multiplication to `95.44×` for arithmetic-only comparison."
msgstr "両実装がまだオラクルに合格する 1,024 桁では、arithmetic-only の五つの演算について floating GDA は `0.131–16.798 µs/op`、DzmingLi は `12.459–78.978 µs/op` を記録しています。full-path の中央値は `7.427–24.133 µs/op` 対 `152.145–205.549 µs/op` です。その結果、GDA の速度比は arithmetic-only の乗算の `3.54×` から arithmetic-only の比較の `95.44×` までになります。"

#: manual/performance/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:25
msgid "DzmingLi arithmetic is incorrect from 4,096 digits, so those points are not speedups. At 20,000 digits the validated GDA medians are `14.810 µs` add, `15.083 µs` subtract, `60.588 µs` divide, and `0.130 µs` compare for arithmetic-only; full-path medians are `154.468`, `155.582`, `131.363`, and `139.865 µs`, respectively."
msgstr "DzmingLi の算術は 4,096 桁以降で不正なため、その点は speedup として扱いません。20,000 桁の検証済み GDA は arithmetic-only で加算 `14.810`、減算 `15.083`、除算 `60.588`、比較 `0.130 µs/op`、full-path は順に `154.468`、`155.582`、`131.363`、`139.865 µs/op` です。"

#: manual/performance/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:31
msgid "Data-dependent comparison"
msgstr "データに依存する比較"

#: manual/performance/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:33
msgid "DzmingLi's arithmetic-only comparison curve remains data-dependent at large input sizes: its medians at 4,096, 8,192, 10,000, 16,384, and 20,000 digits are `105.918`, `0.103`, `675.705`, `0.101`, and `2,203.063 µs/op`. Some fixtures can be ordered immediately from sign, exponent, or significant-digit metadata, while others require a deep coefficient comparison. The connected curve therefore contains execution-class spikes rather than a single digit-count scaling law. Full-path timing also includes parsing and construction costs; comparison should be evaluated by input class as well as coefficient size."
msgstr "DzmingLi の arithmetic-only 比較は大規模入力でデータ依存の短絡経路を示します。4,096、8,192、10,000、16,384、20,000 桁の中央値は `105.918`、`0.103`、`675.705`、`0.101`、`2,203.063 µs/op` です。符号、指数、有効桁数だけで判定できる fixture と長い係数を深く比較する fixture が混在するためで、単一の桁数スケーリングとして解釈できません。"

#: manual/performance/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:42
#: manual/performance/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:23
msgid "Data and figures"
msgstr "データと図"

#: manual/performance/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:44
msgid "The figures and reports for this analysis are kept in the repository: the [main figure](../../../artifacts/dzmingli_vs_floating/main.svg), the [supplementary figure](../../../artifacts/dzmingli_vs_floating/supplementary.svg), the [scaling report](../../../artifacts/dzmingli_vs_floating/scaling.html) and the [common-digit report](../../../artifacts/dzmingli_vs_floating/common_digits.html), with the JSONL records and the Plot IR beside them."
msgstr "この分析の図とレポートはリポジトリに保存されています：[メイン図](../../../artifacts/dzmingli_vs_floating/main.svg)、[補足図](../../../artifacts/dzmingli_vs_floating/supplementary.svg)、[scaling レポート](../../../artifacts/dzmingli_vs_floating/scaling.html)、[共通桁レポート](../../../artifacts/dzmingli_vs_floating/common_digits.html)。JSONL レコードと Plot IR も同じ場所にあります。"

#: manual/performance/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:1
msgid "floating_vs_decmial_x performance"
msgstr "floating_vs_decmial_x の性能"

#: manual/performance/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:3
msgid "Measurement contract"
msgstr "測定条件"

#: manual/performance/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:5
msgid "This report covers a MoonBit native release run comparing `moonbitlang/x/decimal@0.4.46` and `Luna-Flow/floating/decimal_gda@0.7.1`, taken before the MoonBit 0.10 migration. The module now depends on `moonbitlang/x@0.5.5`; the run has not been repeated with it. Fixture construction, parsing, conversion, correctness checks, and formatting are outside the timed region. `exact_overlap` measures shared mathematical semantics; `x_compatible` also includes 28 fractional digits and truncation toward zero."
msgstr "このレポートは、MoonBit 0.10 への移行前に行った、`moonbitlang/x/decimal@0.4.46` と `Luna-Flow/floating/decimal_gda@0.7.1` を比較する MoonBit native リリースビルドでの実行を扱います。モジュールは現在 `moonbitlang/x@0.5.5` に依存していますが、それでの再実行はしていません。フィクスチャの構築、解析、変換、正しさの検査、書式化は計時領域の外です。`exact_overlap` は共通の数学的意味論を計測し、`x_compatible` は小数 28 桁と 0 方向への切り捨ても含みます。"

#: manual/performance/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:9
msgid "**Add/subtract:** GDA leads at 1–256 digits (`0.23–0.39 µs/op` versus X's `0.46–0.66 µs/op`); X leads at 1,024–4,096 digits and is about `1.4–1.8×` faster at the upper end."
msgstr "**加減算**：1–256 桁では GDA が優位（`0.23–0.39 µs/op` 対 X の `0.46–0.66 µs/op`）。1,024–4,096 桁では X が逆転し、上限側で約 `1.4–1.8×` 高速です。"

#: manual/performance/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:10
msgid "**Multiply:** For `exact_overlap`, X leads at every scaling point by about `2.1–2.7×`, a constant-factor advantage in this workload rather than evidence of a different complexity class. For `x_compatible`, where both sides also truncate to 28 fractional digits, GDA leads by about `1.8–2.1×` at 1–64 digits, the two are equivalent at 256 digits, and X leads by about `1.9–2.3×` at 1,024–4,096 digits."
msgstr "**乗算：** `exact_overlap` では X がすべてのスケーリング点で約 `2.1–2.7×` 速く、これはこのワークロードにおける定数倍の優位であって、計算量のクラスが異なる証拠ではありません。両側とも小数部 28 桁への切り捨ても行う `x_compatible` では、1–64 桁で GDA が約 `1.8–2.1×` 速く、256 桁では両者が同等、1,024–4,096 桁では X が約 `1.9–2.3×` 速くなります。"

#: manual/performance/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:11
msgid "**Divide:** For `exact_overlap`, GDA leads by `1.2–4.1×` at 1–64 digits, while X leads by `1.3–3.4×` at 256–4,096 digits. In `x_compatible`, the two implementations stay within about `1.2×` through 256 digits, then GDA leads by about `1.8×` at 1,024 and `3.8×` at 4,096 digits."
msgstr "**除算**：`exact_overlap` では 1–64 桁で GDA が約 `1.2–4.1×` 高速、256–4,096 桁では X が約 `1.3–3.4×` 高速です。`x_compatible` は 256 桁まで約 `1.2×` 以内で、1,024 桁と 4,096 桁では GDA がそれぞれ約 `1.8×`、`3.8×` 高速です。"

#: manual/performance/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:12
msgid "**Divide caveat:** from 64 digits on, the `x_compatible` fixtures round the GDA operands to the division precision (at most 51 digits) while X divides the full operands, so these GDA timings measure less work; see the [known limitation](../design/floating_vs_decmial_x.md#known-limitation-operand-rounding-in-x-compatible-division). The 1–16-digit points and the whole common-digit run are not affected."
msgstr "**除算の注意：** 64 桁以降、`x_compatible` のフィクスチャは GDA のオペランドを除算の精度（高々 51 桁）に丸める一方、X はオペランド全体を割るので、これらの GDA の計時は少ない仕事量を測っています。[既知の制限](../design/floating_vs_decmial_x.md#known-limitation-operand-rounding-in-x-compatible-division)を参照してください。1〜16 桁の点と、一般的な桁数の実行全体は影響を受けません。"

#: manual/performance/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:13
msgid "**Compare:** GDA leads at every scaling point, from about `3.4×` at 1 digit to `14.8×` at 4,096 digits, consistent with early sign/coefficient-length/exponent shortcuts."
msgstr "**比較**：全サイズで GDA が高速で、1 桁の約 `3.4×` から 4,096 桁の約 `14.8×` まで差が広がります。符号・係数長・指数による早期判定が影響します。"

#: manual/performance/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:15
msgid "Cross-implementation context"
msgstr "他実装との位置付け"

#: manual/performance/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:17
msgid "Fixed-precision decimal64/128 is often fastest within its bound. Arbitrary-precision add/subtract is commonly near `O(n)`, while multiply/divide depend on BigInt algorithms and thresholds. Mature C implementations may benefit from limb layout and SIMD/assembly. Full IEEE/GDA contexts pay for rounding, status flags, and special values."
msgstr "固定精度 decimal64/128 は範囲内で高速、任意精度の加減算は概ね `O(n)`、乗除算は BigInt のアルゴリズムと閾値に依存します。成熟した C 実装は limb 配置や SIMD/アセンブリの恩恵を受け、完全な IEEE/GDA コンテキストは丸め・状態フラグ・特殊値のコストを伴います。"

#: manual/performance/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:19
msgid "Conclusion and limits"
msgstr "結論と限界"

#: manual/performance/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:21
msgid "For this workload, X favors simple high-throughput arithmetic; GDA favors explicit precision, rounding, and context semantics. Only `exact_overlap` multiplication keeps a roughly constant ratio across sizes, which points to a constant-factor gap there. Add, subtract, `exact_overlap` divide and `x_compatible` multiply cross over from GDA to X as the digits grow, and compare moves from about `3.4×` to `14.8×` in GDA's favour, so for those operations the two libraries have different fixed and per-digit costs rather than a constant ratio; larger BigInt sizes may expose further thresholds. Other GDA implementations may have similar overhead with similar algorithms, but limb layout, caching, native code, fixed precision, or hardware can change constants; the standard does not prescribe an algorithm. Neighbouring sizes average over different scale pairs, because the scale profile rotates with the global dataset id (see the [scaling executable design](../design/floating_vs_decmial_x/bench.md)), so a single step of a curve mixes size and scale effects. Results are specific to these fixtures, target, build mode, and host. Recheck JSONL and `artifacts/` reports. This benchmark remains GitHub-only and is not published to Mooncakes."
msgstr "このワークロードでは、X は単純で高スループットな算術に向き、GDA は明示的な精度、丸め、コンテキストの意味論に向いています。サイズを通じてほぼ一定の比を保つのは `exact_overlap` の乗算だけで、そこでは定数倍の差を示しています。加算、減算、`exact_overlap` の除算、`x_compatible` の乗算は桁数が増えるにつれて GDA 優位から X 優位に入れ替わり、比較は GDA 有利のまま約 `3.4×` から `14.8×` へ広がります。したがってこれらの演算では、二つのライブラリは一定の比ではなく、固定コストと桁あたりのコストが異なります。さらに大きな BigInt サイズでは別のしきい値が現れるかもしれません。他の GDA 実装も同様のアルゴリズムなら同程度のオーバーヘッドを持つかもしれませんが、リムの配置、キャッシュ、ネイティブコード、固定精度、ハードウェアによって定数は変わります。標準はアルゴリズムを定めていません。スケールのプロファイルが全体のデータセット id とともに入れ替わるため（[スケーリング用実行ファイルの設計](../design/floating_vs_decmial_x/bench.md)を参照）、隣り合うサイズは異なるスケールの組で平均されており、曲線の一段にはサイズとスケールの効果が混ざっています。結果はこれらのフィクスチャ、ターゲット、ビルドモード、ホストに固有です。JSONL と `artifacts/` のレポートで確認してください。このベンチマークは引き続き GitHub だけで提供し、Mooncakes には公開しません。"

#: manual/performance/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:25
msgid "The figures and reports for this analysis are kept in the repository: the [main figure](../../../artifacts/floating_vs_decmial_x/main.svg), the [scaling report](../../../artifacts/floating_vs_decmial_x/scaling.html) and the [common-digit report](../../../artifacts/floating_vs_decmial_x/common_digits.html), with the JSONL records and the Plot IR beside them."
msgstr "この分析の図とレポートはリポジトリに保存されています：[メイン図](../../../artifacts/floating_vs_decmial_x/main.svg)、[scaling レポート](../../../artifacts/floating_vs_decmial_x/scaling.html)、[共通桁レポート](../../../artifacts/floating_vs_decmial_x/common_digits.html)。JSONL レコードと Plot IR も同じ場所にあります。"

